Description: self-extensible AI coding agent for the terminal
 Pi is an interactive coding agent that runs in your terminal. It reads,
 edits, and writes files, runs shell commands, and manages persistent
 sessions, driving a large language model through a tool-calling loop to
 carry out software engineering tasks.
 .
 It talks to many model providers through a single unified API, including
 OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Mistral, Amazon Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, and
 GitHub Copilot, and can be extended at runtime with custom tools, skills,
 prompt templates, and themes.
 .
 This package installs the "pi" command. Provider API keys are supplied at
 runtime through environment variables or the interactive setup; none are
 required to install the package.
